{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559990-sphere-immunities","id":1559990,"title":"Sphere Immunities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-15T10:29:57-07:00","id":1559990,"title":"Sphere Immunities","content":"Time 5 has an effect called Time Immunity. While this presumably can be set up as a defense against incoming Time effects, it also specifically mentions making the caster or others immune to time's passage. Time 5 can defend against the subject of the Sphere itself.<br /> <br /> Now, to me, there is no reason this would be a unique property of the Time Sphere. Likely all rank 5 Spheres have some kind of immunity effect against things within the domain of the sphere, which does make sense for rank 5. It makes sense that Forces 5 could put together an immunity to fire effect. Or an immunity to gravity effect. It also makes sense that a Matter master could make himself immune to swords or steel.<br /> <br /> Now I'm trying to work through any issues with this and what kind of guidelines there would need to be. There are a number of instant kill options, some even catastrophically explosive, but effects of that type already exist at rank 5. There are some things where I can't even envision what the effect would be (like immunity to distance), but I use the unwritten rule that if neither the player or the ST can describe what an effect would be, there is no effect. <br /> <br /> What is the most broken application you can think of?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T10:56:08-07:00","id":1559991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some things where I can't even envision what the effect would be (like immunity to distance), but I use the unwritten rule that if neither the player or the ST can describe what an effect would be, there is no effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Corr 4 let's you to put things on a &quot;place outside of space&quot;. I could imagine a lvl 5 version of that could let you exists &quot;outside of space&quot;, but &quot;move&quot;. Prob. needs to use Corr 2 to see outside the &quot;subspace&quot;. And I would rule the movement runs more along the Correspondence table than walking...Maybe you can go to &quot;line of sight&quot; as part of a single action, but need more time to move to other ranges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T13:49:41-07:00","id":1559992,"title":"","content":"I think there is a relatively (no pun intended) unique aspect of what time &quot;is&quot; compared to the purviews of the other Spheres that lets Time Immunity make sense as a distinct effect. Time is just time. There aren't time particles (at least beyond some sci-fi conjectures and unsupported hypotheses in quantum mechanics). Time is a continuous dimension with no observable units. You can't measure &quot;time&quot; in an object by measuring something about time. You can arbitrarily create units of time, and use constants in nature to say X number of those units has occurred so a given object is X units &quot;old.&quot; But that's not really the time of the object in a tangible sense.<br /> <br /> Every Sphere is meant to defend the mage against the subject of the Sphere, but it tends to get more chopped up into more effects. As said, you don't make yourself immune to Matter (what does that even mean since we're made of Matter?) you render steel unable to harm you. Mind 1 lets you make Mind Shields. The Correspondence example Aleph pointed out. Etc. The concept of outright immunity gets complicated simply by the virtue of (at least in the setting of Mage) the majority of Spheres are all things mages themselves are defined as being made out of.<br /> <br /> It's easy to say a Master of Life can have a spell that makes them immune to other Life spells (or at least someone would have to vastly out roll them under the counter-magic rules, but AFAIK that applies to Time Immunity as well), but it's not easy to figure out being immune to &quot;life&quot; would be for a living thing. Does it make them effectively dead (and thus potentially weak to Matter mages)? Does it make them not-alive but not dead either? If so what does that even do as a meaningful distinction? There's no readily available concept like &quot;freezing time&quot; we can appeal to.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> As for the most broken application, it's hard to say without having a grasp of what it would mean.<br /> <br /> That said, considering you can do it at Forces 2, having gravity stop applying to a target on Earth for one turn is basically an instant kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T15:14:17-07:00","id":1559994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559990-sphere-immunities?p=1559992#post1559992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Sphere is meant to defend the mage against the subject of the Sphere, but it tends to get more chopped up into more effects. As said, you don't make yourself immune to Matter (what does that even mean since we're made of Matter?) you render steel unable to harm you. Mind 1 lets you make Mind Shields. The Correspondence example Aleph pointed out. Etc. The concept of outright immunity gets complicated simply by the virtue of (at least in the setting of Mage) the majority of Spheres are all things mages themselves are defined as being made out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that perspective; level 5 powers tend to be the point where a Mage begins to transcend the nature of a Sphere's subject. The most unique property of Time is the inherent forward momentum, and Time Immunity is the point where they can truly escape that - they can twist and bend it before, but not really escape it. So immunity as an effect may be more the consequence of the Time Sphere's nature rather than the position at level 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T09:16:36-07:00","id":1560063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559990-sphere-immunities?p=1559992#post1559992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Sphere is meant to defend the mage against the subject of the Sphere, but it tends to get more chopped up into more effects. As said, you don't make yourself immune to Matter (what does that even mean since we're made of Matter?) you render steel unable to harm you. Mind 1 lets you make Mind Shields. The Correspondence example Aleph pointed out. Etc. The concept of outright immunity gets complicated simply by the virtue of (at least in the setting of Mage) the majority of Spheres are all things mages themselves are defined as being made out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense that would need to be explicit, yes. Most immunity effects would need to be pared down, not just for balance sake but also for utility sake. Immunity to the full domain of many spheres is either nonsensical or counterproductive. Likely we'd also need to state that Masters of a Sphere are familiar enough with the domain that they can compensate for obvious unintended consequences. Immunity to stone can probably allow phasing through walls while not causing the mage to plummet through the floor. <br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the most broken application, it's hard to say without having a grasp of what it would mean.<br /> <br /> That said, considering you can do it at Forces 2, having gravity stop applying to a target on Earth for one turn is basically an instant kill. </div> </div> </div>I had considered what immunity to the strong nuclear force would do. Most likely explosive dissolution on the order of nuclear weaponry, which is quite powerful, but also on par with what can be done with Matter 5.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T10:22:25-07:00","id":1560065,"title":"","content":"I think that strains the concept of &quot;immunity&quot; to the point of it being unproductive to call it that. For example, I think it would be far more useful to consider it a standard Mastery level effect to have &quot;conditional interaction,&quot; with the subject of the Sphere in question. So you could make yourself intangible and move through things, but that comes with the risk of falling through floors if they're made of the same type of Matter as the walls you want to walk through. At Mastery you can make it conditional to avoid that problem.<br /> <br /> I think as an issue of communication it just handles what we're talking about better than &quot;immunity&quot; does. <br /> <br /> The reason I opted for my gravity example is because other forces that are acting on us all the time but are essentially moot because of the gravitation of Earth still apply in simple predictable ways if you are rendered immune to gravity for even a few seconds; it's simple to figure out what &quot;immunity&quot; to gravity would do if you didn't account for anything else and/or wanted those forces to take over. Even if we had a quantum physicist here that could get into the math, it's not easy to predict what would happen if you turned off the strong nuclear force in an object (and hopefully without a lecture on why they call it the strong interaction, not a force, these days). Yes, the weak nuclear force would be significantly less opposed and thus expected decay rates would increase, but electromagnetic and gravitational impacts would be more influential as well and would moderate against decay. I have a strong (sigh, no pun intended) feeling that an physicist would give us more of a probabilistic answer than a binary answer on if that would result in fast enough decay to achieve fission-like energetic release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T11:53:20-07:00","id":1560068,"title":"","content":"That's also true for Time. Time Immunity allows you to move while the flow of time it's frozen. But one could equally imagine something static and incappable of change as what &quot;immune to time&quot; means (like data on a graph that doesn't change it's value with the &quot;time axis&quot; - that object would effectively be &quot;immune to time&quot; to a point the time axis can be omited as it doesn't affect it at all).<br /> <br /> It comes to mind the D&amp;D joke on the &quot;immovable rod&quot;, that on deploy should ascelerate immediately, as it's fixed on &quot;a point of space&quot; but the planet isn't <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Ultimately a Master of Time it's free to choose how to interact with the time flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T14:28:51-07:00","id":1560078,"title":"","content":"That kinda goes back to my first point about time fundamentally being different from what the other Spheres govern. Though I feel like this gets unproductive because there's a big difference between how time actually works according to our current models of physics, and how time works practically for our lived experiences. Ultimately we want systems that create magical effects that match the fantasy conceits of the game; not a physics debate. Time Immunity is a more coherent mental concept for the goal of a magical effect than Life Immunity would be; which is certainly informed by our modern scientific understanding of time and biology, but the game isn't bound strictly to that perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T09:17:02-07:00","id":1560096,"title":"","content":"Another problem that surges it's that sometimes this sort of things could be defined as the purview of <i>several Spheres </i>(which could be bad<i>, </i>because then we're messing with how the objects in the system interact with each other).<br /> <br /> I.E:<br /> <br /> &quot;Counting as dead&quot;, as suggested for &quot;Life Immunity&quot; sounds similar to the necrosynthesis effects that combine Matter and Life to give &quot;properties&quot; of being undead. Being &quot;impervious to Iron&quot;, as suggested for Matter, it's sort of crossing paths with how Wards and Bans limit interaction between objects.<br /> <br /> Granted, in both cases it's not *exactly the same*, but one could argue that not all Spheres really allow to change your relationship with the subject by themselves.<br /> <br /> Time has effects &quot;changing your relationship with the subject&quot; at levels far below 5, like with &quot;rewind time&quot; at 3, or ascelerating yourself. Time does that because everyone and everything on Mage exists within a sort of &quot;personal time&quot; that can be selected and manipulated. Matter doesn't do that because you're not a &quot;matter pattern&quot;.<br /> <br /> When I think about Mastery giving you &quot;Matter Immunity&quot;, it immediately comes to mind either the effect that allows you to choose how matter interacts with each other (bullets that can pass trough armor was the example) or even the &quot;Adamantium rote&quot; that makes stuff &quot;almost indestructible&quot; (whatever that means). But RAW that wouldn't do nothing for the mage - unless, maybe, you add Life.<br /> <br /> I believe a Life 4/5 + Matter 5 effect could very well combine &quot;shapeshifting&quot; and &quot;exotic matter&quot; to make one &quot;nearly insubstantial&quot;. That could make you &quot;immune to all matter&quot; (and living beings?), but you better add some limitations or extra effects to that, if you don't want to see how Earth's core looks like (well, you would die of heat, pressure, etc. before that - not immune to Forces). You also want to breathe, but the transformation could take care of those little issues.<br /> <br /> In any case, I don't think Matter alone can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-19-2026, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T14:30:27-07:00","id":1560100,"title":"","content":"The question, I suppose, is if the Immunity effect is changing the target's pattern or not. If it is, then sure Life is needed, but it doesn't sound like the pattern itself is changing. It doesn't appear to be for Time Immunity, since there are no extra spheres mentioned. Possibly it is a locked effect as Mage does sometimes forget to mention that.<br /> <br /> Of course as you say, Time is changing someone's relationship to Time... but I still don't see that the Matter Immunity requires changing a life pattern to work. At least not in your insubstantiality example. If Matter 5 can make a substance insubstantial when it overlaps with the area of the effect then at most you need Life 2 to anchor the effect to the person. Possibly the effect can only be made permanent (in the 'spell is over, this is just the new normal' sense) if the effect is grafted into the target pattern, but that's pure speculation. M20 doesn't give guidelines on what that kind of permanence requires, because it isn't even clear that kind of permanence is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-22T06:59:16-07:00","id":1560150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559990-sphere-immunities#post1559990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 5 has an effect called Time Immunity. While this presumably can be set up as a defense against incoming Time effects, it also specifically mentions making the caster or others immune to time's passage. Time 5 can defend against the subject of the Sphere itself.<br /> <br /> Now, to me, there is no reason this would be a unique property of the Time Sphere. Likely all rank 5 Spheres have some kind of immunity effect against things within the domain of the sphere, which does make sense for rank 5. It makes sense that Forces 5 could put together an immunity to fire effect. Or an immunity to gravity effect. It also makes sense that a Matter master could make himself immune to swords or steel.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you need 5 ranks in the Sphere of Forces to obtain immunity, you're probably the laughing stock of the arch mage community.<br /> <br /> That's a problem that ceases to exist the moment you obtain the power to shut down the flow of energy and stop it from working.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559990-sphere-immunities#post1559990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some things where I can't even envision what the effect would be (like immunity to distance),<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have you heard of Saturo Gojo?<br /> <br /> He's a character in Jujutsu Kaisen, who is virtually untouchable in combat, because he has a curse technique that increases the amount of distance between him and his opponent's attacks by an infinite magnitude. Regardless of how fast they move, or how strong they are, it doesn't matter if they are unable to actually reach him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559990-sphere-immunities#post1559990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the most broken application you can think of?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Life Sphere 5 - True Immortality: At what point do the atomic particles and quarks that make up the building blocks of life become sentient matter? Why do some atoms form themselves into flesh, while others become plants, fungi, rocks, liquids, est.? What stops the molecules in your body from trying to replicate, or assimilate the molecular composition of somebody else? What makes you an individual, if we're all composed of the same fundamental substances?<br /> <br /> A master of of the Life sphere should be able to answer these questions, identify the processes involved, and achieve full, absolute control over bodies at the sub-atomic level. Thereby allowing them to survive and regenerate from literally anything. If a piece of them is destroyed beyond repair, they can just assimilate the atomic particles from their surroundings in order to create a functional replacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 05-23-2026, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}